  "raw": " everything began to lag behind. After as long a time as is needed the current player begins to seem irredeemably bad, and by a decided margin the campaign doesn't continue.  Welcome back.\nThis was good writing. I didn't even see it coming or know what kind of game would make use of this storyline. That being said anyone playing with this character is going have a very different experience than any other group because they will witness the light vs. darkness dilemma in its entirety as well.\nNot everyone will understand that their old school nerd's radio show concept had nothing to do with it, though, so there may be confusion if the entry is poorly written. In fact, I think that requesting something new is probably best for building (a) a group.",
  "serialized": "everything began to lag behind. After as long a time as is needed the current player begins to seem irredeemably bad, and by a decided margin the campaign doesn't continue. Welcome back. This was good writing. I didn't even see it coming or know what kind of game would make use of this storyline. That being said anyone playing with this character is going have a very different experience than any other group because they will witness the light vs. darkness dilemma in its entirety as well. Not everyone will understand that their old school nerd's radio show concept had nothing to do with it, though, so there may be confusion if the entry is poorly written. In fact, I think that requesting something new is probably best for building (a) a group.",
